==Icelandic==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|non|is}} {{term|vinr|lang=non}}, {{etyl|gem-pro|fo}} {{recons|winiz|lang=gem-pro}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈvɪːnʏr/|lang=is}}
*: {{rhymes|ɪːnʏr|lang=is}}

===Noun===
{{is-noun|m|vinar|vinir}}

# a [[friend]]{{jump|is|friend|d|s}}
#: ''Þú ert '''vinur''' minn.''
#:: You are my '''friend'''.
#: ''Þú ert góður '''vinur'''.''
#:: You are a good '''friend'''.
# {{context|colloquial|slang|often used with a definite article|lang=is}} [[mate]], [[lad]], an affectionate moniker for a close [[friend]] or [[pal]], especially used as a form of [[address]]{{jump|is|mate|s}}
#: ''[[jæja|Jæja]] '''vinurinn''', ætli maður fari ekki að [[koma sér af stað]].''
#:: Well '''mate''', I guess one should [[get going]].

====Declension====
{{is-decl-noun-m-s3|v|i|n|i=?i}}

